1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,295
This is Joker Chess, a new chess variant that's gaining popularity.

2
00:00:04,345 --> 00:00:10,060
It's regular chess with one extra move per player, and that move changes how the whole game feels.

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:14,279
Once per game, instead of a normal move, you can make a Joker Move.

4
00:00:14,299 --> 00:00:18,221
Your queen, rook, bishop or knight jumps to any empty square.

5
00:00:18,271 --> 00:00:20,008
Kings and pawns can't jump.

6
00:00:20,058 --> 00:00:24,435
The jump can't capture and can't give check, and your own king must be safe after it.

7
00:00:24,635 --> 00:00:26,526
Everything else is regular chess.

8
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:31,418
With that jump, your rook can land on an open file and threaten mate on the back rank.

9
00:00:31,568 --> 00:00:35,077
The jump can't give check, so the other side gets one move to answer.

10
00:00:35,577 --> 00:00:38,969
Your rook can also land on the king's file and pin the queen.

11
00:00:39,869 --> 00:00:41,853
Your bishop can do the same on a diagonal.

12
00:00:42,753 --> 00:00:45,963
Your knight can land where it hits the queen and a rook at once.

13
00:00:46,863 --> 00:00:50,107
And a knight can land near the king, so the mate can't be stopped.

14
00:00:51,707 --> 00:00:53,722
All of this can happen to you too.

15
00:00:53,822 --> 00:00:58,697
While your opponent still has their Joker, any empty square can hide a fork or a mating threat.

16
00:00:58,747 --> 00:01:00,532
But your own Joker can get you out.

17
00:01:00,582 --> 00:01:04,511
If their rook pins your queen, your rook can jump into the line and save it.

18
00:01:05,411 --> 00:01:08,674
And when a check would be mate, a rook can jump in and block it.

19
00:01:09,024 --> 00:01:13,758
So the tension stays on, and every move counts while at least one Joker is left.

20
00:01:13,858 --> 00:01:18,344
Even when you're losing, you're still in the game, because one jump can turn it around.

21
00:01:19,444 --> 00:01:24,781
The developers estimate that a Joker still in hand is worth about 150 rating points on average.

22
00:01:24,831 --> 00:01:28,214
That's a real edge, though a beginner still won't beat a grandmaster.

23
00:01:28,414 --> 00:01:34,202
On the first move, White has 20 options in regular chess and 240 with the Joker Move.

24
00:01:34,452 --> 00:01:43,720
After two moves each, 197 thousand possible games become over 114 million, almost 580 times more.

25
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:46,342
So memorized openings run out much sooner.

26
00:01:46,842 --> 00:01:51,055
Players say it's more gripping than regular chess, and that it's hard to go back after it.

27
00:01:51,305 --> 00:01:55,132
The app is free, and you can play right now, alone or with other people.

28
00:01:55,232 --> 00:01:58,637
Bots need no sign-up, and a friend joins with a four-digit code.

29
00:01:58,787 --> 00:02:01,516
Online, a rated game starts within seconds.

30
00:02:01,716 --> 00:02:05,053
The developers also built their own engine for Joker Chess.

31
00:02:05,203 --> 00:02:07,944
After every game, it gives you a free review.

32
00:02:07,994 --> 00:02:12,363
It shows each Joker Move that was missed, and how much it would have changed the game.

33
00:02:12,613 --> 00:02:14,505
And the puzzles train you to find them.

34
00:02:14,855 --> 00:02:19,131
Joker Chess is on the App Store and Google Play, and the community keeps growing.
